## 8. Automation & Event-Driven Rules (MANDATORY)

### ERP Automations
| Lifecycle Event | Required Automation | Implementation |
|---|---|---|
| **Employee Created** | Trigger onboarding checklist | `setImmediate` after `COMMIT` |
| **Candidate Hired** | Trigger onboarding | `setImmediate`, `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` |
| **All Onboarding Complete** | Auto-close checklist | After `PUT /onboarding/tasks/:taskId`, count remaining |
| **Employee Exit** | Reassign CRM leads + OMS | `UPDATE leads SET assigned_to = manager_id` |
| **Payroll Run** | Post to GL | `ledgerHelper.processVoucher()` in transaction |
| **Asset Allocated** | Decrement inventory | `ledgerHelper.postToStockLedger(OUT)` |
| **Attendance Anomaly** | Log to compliance | Async after mutation |

### MR Tracker Automations
| Lifecycle Event | Required Automation | Implementation |
|---|---|---|
| **Visit Completed** | Recalc performance score | `setImmediate` → refresh `monthly_mr_metrics` view or update in-memory cache |
| **New Visit Scheduled** | Check Tier A coverage | Alert if Tier A entity > 14 days without visit |
| **Lead Converted** | Create visit record + commission | `POST /api/visits` + `POST /api/commissions` in transaction |
| **Month Rollover** | Archive prior month metrics | Cron at 00:01 on 1st — copy view snapshot to `mr_performance_history` |
| **MR Territory Changed** | Reassign entities + visits | Cascade update `assigned_mr_id` on doctors/pharmacies/hospitals |

### Automation Coding Standards
- Use `setImmediate(async () => { try { ... } catch(e) { console.error(e) } })` for non-blocking side effects.
- Every automation MUST be idempotent — `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING` or existence checks.
- Automation failures MUST be logged, MUST NOT bubble to HTTP response.
- Each automation MUST have a dedicated integration test.

