## 17. Performance Standards

### Backend
- `/api/monthly-metrics` must respond in < 500ms
- All list endpoints must respond in < 200ms
- Complex JOIN queries must use `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` during development
- Required indexes: `visit_schedules(mr_id, scheduled_date)`, `medical_representatives(status)`, `pcd_transactions(mr_id)`, `doctors(territory)`, `pharmacies(territory)`

### Frontend
- Dashboard components must show skeleton/loading state within 100ms of mount
- All charts must use `debounce={50}` on `ResponsiveContainer`
- Lazy-load all non-critical components with `React.lazy` + `Suspense`
- Widget preferences persisted in `localStorage` — never re-fetch unless user triggers refresh

### In-Memory Data
- In-memory fallback must ALWAYS return plausible data for the REQUESTED month
- If < 5 visits exist for the requested month, generate synthetic visits using entity/MR seed data
- Synthetic visits are clearly marked: `{ ..., is_synthetic: true, notes: 'Auto-generated for demo' }`

