## 17. AI Performance Dashboard Rules (MR Tracker — MANDATORY)

### A. Data Sourcing — DB First, Memory Fallback
- ALWAYS query `ai_recommendations`, `sentiment_analysis`, `competitor_mentions` from PostgreSQL when `dbReady === true`
- If DB returns 0 rows (empty tables), DO NOT fall back to memory silently — log a warning and still return the DB result
- Seed SQL lives in `src/database/seed_ai_performance.sql` — run it once after DB creation
- Never compute metrics from in-memory seed data when DB is available

### B. `/api/ai-performance` Endpoint Contract
Returns these fields (ALL required — never omit):
```typescript
{
  total_recommendations,  // number
  adoption_rate,          // 0-100 %
  success_rate,           // 0-100 % (of acted-upon recs)
  conversion_rate,        // 0-100 % (of acted-upon recs)
  avg_time_to_action,     // hours (integer)
  acted_upon,             // count
  pending_actions,        // count = total - acted_upon
  revenue_impact,         // INR extracted from outcome_details
  by_type,                // TypeBreakdown[] sorted by total DESC
  leaderboard,            // MRLeaderboardRow[] sorted by adoption_rate DESC
  weekly_trend,           // WeeklyTrend[8] — last 8 weeks always
  outcome_dist,           // { converted, positive, neutral, negative, pending }
  erp_sync,               // { leads_total, leads_converted, sales_total, sales_value }
  date_range,             // { from: YYYY-MM-DD, to: YYYY-MM-DD }
  generated_at,           // ISO timestamp
}
```
- `outcome_dist` values MUST sum to `total_recommendations` — test this invariant
- `acted_upon + pending_actions` MUST equal `total_recommendations`
- Accepts `?from=YYYY-MM-DD&to=YYYY-MM-DD&mr_id=N` query params
- Leaderboard MUST be sorted descending by `adoption_rate`

### C. "Mark Action Taken" Automation
- `PATCH /api/ai-recommendations/:id` with `{ mr_action_taken: true, action_taken_at: ISO_STRING }`
- After marking, the next `/api/ai-performance` call MUST show updated `adoption_rate`
- Trigger side effect: if outcome is 'converted', recalculate `revenue_impact`

### D. Component Rules
- Use `Promise.allSettled` for all 4 parallel fetches — never `Promise.all` (single failure kills dashboard)
- Auto-refresh every 60 seconds via `setInterval` in `useEffect` — clear interval on unmount
- All 4 KPI values MUST show real percentages — never 0% when `total_recommendations > 0`
- Tab state persists until user manually switches — never auto-switch tabs
- "Mark Done" button shows spinner during PATCH, re-fetches metrics after success

### E. ERP Sync Rules
- `erp_sync.sales_value` comes from `SUM(sales.total_amount)` — never hardcoded
- If `leads` or `sales` tables don't exist (non-fatal), return zeros with no crash
- ERP sync banner visible only when `leads_total > 0 OR sales_total > 0`

### F. Testing Invariants (assert in all test tiers)
1. `adoption_rate > 0` when seeded data exists
2. `acted_upon + pending_actions === total_recommendations`
3. `outcome_dist` values sum to `total_recommendations`
4. `leaderboard` sorted descending by `adoption_rate`
5. `weekly_trend` always has exactly 8 entries
6. `sentiment_score` between 0-100 for all sentiment records
7. `sentiment` in `['threat', 'opportunity', 'price_sensitive']` for all competitor mentions

