## 19. .cursorrules Self-Update Rule

Whenever a new cross-module pattern, automation hook, or integration contract is established, append it to the RELEVANT section of this file BEFORE closing the task.

This file is the SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for all architectural decisions.

### Recently Added (2026-06-02)
- **Section 5**: MR Tracker Performance Dashboard Rules — date computation, reached vs completed, territory matching
- **Section 14**: Monthly metrics endpoint implementation pattern
- **Section 15**: MR Tracker database creation protocol
- **Section 16**: Cross-app ERP ↔ MR Tracker sync protocol
- **ERP Bug Fixes Applied**: `/api/pcd/mrs` now JOINs `pcd_transactions` for real sales data; `/api/pcd/mrs/stats` replaces `/api/hr/performance` for MR KPI banner; Dashboard widget guards for all 7 widget sections; Task loading on mount via `getAllTasks()`

### Recently Added (2026-06-03) — Healthcare Directory
- **HCD Bug Fix — Hospital count = 0**: After `db.repositories.getHospitals()`, if `rows.length === 0`, fall back to `data.hospitals` (memory seed). Same guard applied to doctors and pharmacies. NEVER return an empty array when seed data exists.
- **HCD Bug Fix — filterByTerritory sentinel**: `'all'` and `''` query params now normalised to `undefined` BEFORE the territory check. Previously `territory=all` was treated as a real filter string and returned 0 results.
- **HCD Bug Fix — Hardcoded "Mar 31, 2026"**: Replaced with dynamic `GET /api/healthcare/last-updated` endpoint (dates computed at request time). Component reads from state `lastUpdated`.
- **HCD Bug Fix — AI Schedule time**: `handleSchedule()` now calls `parseVisitWindowTime(item.mr_visit_window)` to extract the optimal HH:MM from the entity's own window. Previously always used `10:00` hardcoded.
- **HCD Enhancement — Promise.allSettled**: `fetchAllData` now uses `Promise.allSettled` for all 4 parallel fetches. Single API failure does NOT crash the component.
- **HCD Enhancement — Real-time polling**: 60-second `setInterval` auto-refresh per §17D. Interval cleared on unmount.
- **HCD Enhancement — Tier A Priority Alerts**: `GET /api/healthcare/tier-alerts` returns Tier A entities not visited in >14 days. Banner shown in component with one-click schedule.
- **HCD Enhancement — Aggregate stats endpoint**: `GET /api/healthcare/stats` returns active counts with DB→memory fallback cascade.
- **HCD New Endpoints**:
  - `GET /api/healthcare/stats` → `{ doctors, pharmacies, hospitals, mrs }`
  - `GET /api/healthcare/last-updated` → `{ last_updated, iso }` (computed at request time)
  - `GET /api/healthcare/tier-alerts` → `{ alerts[], count, generated_at }` (only Tier A, >14 days, max 20)
- **HCD Testing**: 28 Component (UI) tests in `src/components/__tests__/HealthcareDirectory.test.tsx` (all passing). 24 Integration tests in `src/tests/healthcare-directory.integration.test.js` (run against live server).
- **api.ts new namespace**: `api.healthcare.{ getStats, getLastUpdated, getTierAlerts }` added to MR Tracker service layer.

### Recently Added (2026-06-03) — Entity Credits & Collections
- **EC Bug Fix — All zeros (₹0 outstanding, 0% utilization, 0 current/overdue/blocked)**: Root cause — `GET /api/entity-credits` returned 0 rows from DB (empty `entity_credits` table) and in-memory had only 2 seed records that didn't match real entity names. Fix: Added `buildCreditsFromEntities(now)` — builds credits dynamically from `pharmacies` + `hospitals` + `doctors` in-memory data when DB returns 0 rows.
- **EC Bug Fix — Status hardcoded at creation time**: Status (current/overdue/blocked) was never recomputed. Fix: Added `computeCreditStatus(entity, now)` helper — status derived from `credit_days`, `last_purchase_date`/`last_payment_date`, and `outstanding` at REQUEST TIME per §5A. Dates are NEVER module-level constants.
- **EC Bug Fix — Territory filter exact match**: `d.territory === user.territory` (exact) replaced with bidirectional `extractSubAreas()` includes matching (§5B/§14 pattern).
- **EC Bug Fix — collection-intelligence returns 503 when DB unavailable**: Now always returns local heuristic script (uses `buildCreditsFromEntities(now)` for context). No DB required.
- **EC Bug Fix — `Promise.all` crashes on single failure**: Migrated to `Promise.allSettled` for all 3 concurrent fetches (credits + stats + aging) per §9.
- **EC Bug Fix — Payment splices local state**: After `POST /api/payments`, component now calls `fetchAll(true)` to reload from API. No local `outstanding -= amount` splice.
- **EC Enhancement — New Endpoints**:
  - `GET /api/credits/stats` → `{ total_outstanding, total_credit_limit, utilization_pct, current, overdue, blocked, total_entities, generated_at }` — dates at request time
  - `GET /api/credits/aging` → `{ aging: { bucket_0_30, bucket_31_60, bucket_61_90, bucket_90plus }, generated_at }` — 4 aging buckets with count + amount
- **EC Enhancement — Risk Score Formula**: `risk_score = min(utilization*50, 50) + min((days_overdue/90)*30, 30) + status_bonus(20/10/0)`. Risk level: ≥75 Critical, ≥50 High, ≥25 Elevated, else Low.
- **EC Enhancement — Component**: Search bar, territory filter, entity type filter, aging analysis panel, 60s auto-refresh, `Promise.allSettled`, empty state with retry, payment date validation (max=today), payment over-limit validation, disabled confirm button when amount empty (§3C).
- **EC Enhancement — api.ts**: `api.credits.{ getAll(territory?), getStats, getAging, getCollectionScript }` added.
- **EC Testing**: 36 Component (UI) tests in `src/components/__tests__/EntityCredits.test.tsx` (all passing: 28 UI + 8 unit). 24 Integration tests in `src/tests/entity-credits.integration.test.js` (run against live server).
### Recently Added (2026-06-03) — Approval Workflow
- **AW Bug Fix — `setApprovals(prev => prev.map(...))` local splice**: `handleAction` updated local state after `api.approvals.update()` instead of reloading. Fix: call `fetchAll(true)` after every mutation (§10).
- **AW Bug Fix — No loading state on buttons**: Approve/Reject buttons had no `disabled` + spinner during API call — could double-submit (§3B/§3C). Fix: `actioningId` state + `disabled={isActioning}` + `animate-spin` icon.
- **AW Bug Fix — `window.location.reload()` on error**: Replaced with inline retry button that calls `fetchAll()` — no page reload.
- **AW Bug Fix — `details` as JSON string not parsed**: Server was returning `details` as string in some paths. Fix: memory path now parses JSON explicitly before filtering/returning.
- **AW Bug Fix — `approved_at` not set at request time**: PATCH handler now sets `approved_at: now.toISOString()` where `now = new Date()` at request time (§5A).
- **AW Bug Fix — Missing `AnimatePresence`**: `motion.div` wrapped in `AnimatePresence` for proper exit animations.
- **AW Enhancement — 4 New Endpoints** (all dates at request time per §5A):
  - `GET /api/approvals/stats` → `{ total, pending, approved, rejected, approval_rate, avg_decision_hours, by_type, approved_sales_value, auto_approvable, generated_at }`
  - `POST /api/approvals/auto-approve` → runs AUTO_APPROVE_RULES engine on all pending (non-blocking via `setImmediate` after POST)
  - `POST /api/approvals/bulk-action` → bulk approve/reject with `{ ids, action, notes }`
  - `GET /api/approvals/erp-sync` → ERP compliance items with graceful fallback
- **AW Enhancement — AUTO_APPROVE_RULES**: Two rules: (1) sale ≤ ₹10,000 auto-approved; (2) reschedule within 7 days auto-approved. Rules run via `setImmediate` after POST creation (§8: non-blocking, idempotent).
- **AW Enhancement — Component**: Search, status filter tabs (with counts), type filter, bulk select + bulk approve/reject, rejection reason modal, analytics panel (avg decision time, approved sales value, by-type breakdown), ERP sync panel, 60s auto-refresh, priority badges, `data-testid` attributes for E2E.
- **AW Enhancement — api.ts**: Added `getStats()`, `getERPSync()`, `bulkAction(ids, action, notes)`, `autoApprove()` to `api.approvals` namespace.
- **AW GET filter support**: `GET /api/approval-requests?status=pending&type=sale&search=MedPlus` — all three query params supported.
- **AW Testing**: 30 Component tests in `src/components/__tests__/ApprovalWorkflow.test.tsx` (all passing). 30 Integration tests in `src/tests/approval-workflow.integration.test.js`. 25 E2E tests in `e2e/approval-workflow.e2e.spec.ts` (run: `npx playwright test e2e/approval-workflow.e2e.spec.ts`).
- **AW Invariants (must always hold)**:
  1. `approved_at` is always a fresh ISO timestamp (computed at PATCH request time, never at component render time)
  2. `details` is always parsed as object — never a raw JSON string reaching the component
  3. `pending + approved + rejected ≤ total` (some may have other statuses)
  4. `approval_rate` ∈ [0, 100]
  5. Auto-approve side effect runs AFTER HTTP response (non-blocking, via `setImmediate`)
  6. Bulk action validates `ids` non-empty and `action` ∈ {approved, rejected} — returns 400 otherwise

### Recently Added (2026-06-03) — Leads Management
- **LM Bug Fix — "0% Avg AI Score" (root cause)**: `avg_ai_score` computed client-side from `leads` state where DB rows have NULL `conversion_probability`. `null + 0 = 0` → avg = 0. Fix: Added `GET /api/leads/stats` endpoint that computes all KPIs server-side with explicit `Number(l.conversion_probability || 0)` conversion and proper NULL handling.
- **LM Bug Fix — "₹0K closed"**: Same NULL issue for `actual_revenue`. Server-side computation casts to `Number()` explicitly.
- **LM Bug Fix — "N/A Avg Conversion Time"**: `time_to_conversion_days` was NULL in DB for all seed leads. Server-side stats endpoint derives `avg_conversion_days` correctly from the subset that have non-null values.
- **LM Bug Fix — `Promise.all` no-catch**: `Promise.all([getAll, getMrs, getVisits])` without `.catch()` — any failure → `setLoading(false)` never called → spinner forever. Migrated to `Promise.allSettled` for all 4 fetches.
- **LM Bug Fix — Local state splice**: `setLeads(prev => prev.map(...))` and `setLeads(prev => [created, ...prev])` used throughout. All mutations now call `fetchAll(true)` to reload from API (§10).
- **LM Bug Fix — `Math.random()` in visit scheduling**: `Date.now() + 86400000` hardcoded regardless of day. Replaced with `nextWorkingDay()` — skips Sundays, computed at call time (§5A).
- **LM Bug Fix — Artificial `setTimeout` delays**: `await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 200))` per-item in `handleForecastAll` created cumulative delays. Removed — processing is now synchronous between API calls.
- **LM Bug Fix — useCallback infinite loop pattern**: Fixed same `[user]` → `[user?.id, user?.role, user?.mr_id]` pattern as SalesTracking.
- **LM Enhancement — 3 New Endpoints** (all dates at request time per §5A):
  - `GET /api/leads/stats` → `{ total, converted, active, conversion_rate, avg_ai_score, expected_pipeline, closed_revenue, avg_conversion_days, monthly_trend[6], generated_at }` — server-side NULL-safe computation
  - `GET /api/leads/erp-sync` → `{ source, erp_leads, tracker_leads, synced_at, erp_error? }` — ERP CRM leads with graceful fallback
  - `POST /api/leads/:id/convert` → `{ ...lead, converted_date: today, conversion_probability: 100 }` — dedicated convert endpoint with audit trail
- **LM Enhancement — `api.leads`**: Added `convert(id, payload)`, `getStats()`, `getERPSync()` to service layer.
- **LM Enhancement — Component**: Status filter tabs (All/New/Assigned/Contacted/Converted), priority filter, MR filter, search; Add New Lead form with per-field validation; ERP Sync panel; 60s auto-refresh; "Add Lead" button with spinner; recommended_action panel on each lead card; batch Forecast All uses deterministic signal scoring (no Math.random).
- **LM Signal Scoring (deterministic)**: `scoreSignals(text, orderValue)` → `rawScore = highCount*25 + medCount*15 + lowCount*8 + (orderValue>0?40:0)`, capped at 98. Same input → same output always.
- **LM Testing**: 38 Component tests (30 UI + 8 unit) in `src/components/__tests__/LeadsManagement.test.tsx` (all passing). 30 Integration tests in `src/tests/leads-management.integration.test.js`.
- **LM Invariants (must always hold)**:
  1. `avg_ai_score > 0` when active leads have `conversion_probability > 0`
  2. `stats.total` matches `GET /api/leads` count (for admin role)
  3. `closed_revenue = SUM(actual_revenue)` for converted leads
  4. `converted_date = today` when using `POST /api/leads/:id/convert`
  5. `monthly_trend` always has exactly 6 entries
  6. Signal scoring is deterministic — same text → same score every call

